`nm -u`: **no** `U c_secret*` / `U c_emit_println` / `U c_guard*`.
`strings`: `c_secret_emit_guard`, `c_secret_refuse_println_ident`,
`c_guard_scan_idents` present.

`c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` has **0 direct `call`s** (89 B wrapper
inlined into guard / check). Symbol is **defined**, not missing.

### Call graph (objdump xrefs)
| Callee | Unique callers |
|--------|----------------|
| `c_secret_emit_guard` | `c_emit_primary_c`, `c_emit_method` |
| `c_emit_println` | `c_emit_ident_stmt` |
| `c_secret_refuse_println_ident` | `c_emit_println` (**1**) |
| `c_guard_scan_idents` | `c_secret_emit_guard` (**1**) |
| `check_secret_println_sinks` | `c_emit_stream_mode`, `llvm_emit_stream`, `run_check_core` |

`c_emit_println` callees: `c_secret_refuse_println_ident` + expr/print
floor. **Zero** `c_secret_emit_guard` / `c_guard_scan_idents`.

Guard **does** compare `println` / `eprintln` / `print_err` / `log` /
`fprintf` / `syslog` (immediates `0x4c4d11`, `0x4c4d10`, `0x4c698f`,
`0x4c69a4`, `0x4c6999`, `0x4c69a1`) then `c_guard_scan_idents`. That
rail is **eprintln / log / expr-position free call / method**, not
stmt `println`.

Host `run_check_core` still calls `check_secret_println_sinks` **after**
typecheck (`0x477505`). WT `check_drive.oo` 12:05 moved secret **before**
type (6.1) — **not in this ELF**.

